{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"pilot","tool":"read_artifact","arguments":{"artifact_id":"source"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"exit_code\": 0, \"stdout\": \"{\\\"action\\\": \\\"read_artifact\\\", \\\"result\\\": {\\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"source\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1, \\\"next_line\\\": null, \\\"total_lines\\\": 15, \\\"text\\\": \\\"% BEGIN EXACT CATALOG SOURCE: prob_13_9\\\\n\\\\\\\\textbf{13.9.} Suppose (X n)n\\\\\\\\geq0 is a sequence of random variables defined on a probability\\\\n\\\\nspace (we take X 0 = 0 as the initial rv.)For n \\\\\\\\geq 1, let\\\\n\\\\nYn \\\\\\\\coloneqqX n -E [Xn\\\\\\\\vertX0,X 1,...,X n- 1].\\\\n\\\\nThe random variable Y n can be interpreted as the new information contained in X n\\\\n\\\\nrelative to the information contained in the past X 0,...,X n- 1Let Sn denote the\\\\n\\\\npartial sum S n \\\\\\\\coloneqqY 1 +Y 2 +\\\\\\\\cdot\\\\\\\\cdot\\\\\\\\cdot+ Yn for n \\\\\\\\geq 1 and S 0 = 0. Show that (S n)n\\\\\\\\geq0 is a\\\\n\\\\nmartingale relative to the filtration (\\\\\\\\sigma(X 1,X 2,...,X n))n\\\\\\\\geq0.\\\\n% END EXACT CATALOG SOURCE: prob_13_9\\\"}, \\\"deadline\\\": {\\\"allowance_seconds\\\": 5400.0, \\\"started_epoch\\\": 1789097537.5854557, \\\"deadline_epoch\\\": 1789102937.5854557, \\\"remaining_seconds\\\": 5384.411511898041}}\\r\\n\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"stdout_sha256\": \"a380a769ec6ad38f4a288af8a740c9867e0725619c7bee632e896e4c344e7e9d\", \"stdout_bytes\": 946, \"stdout_truncated\": false, \"stderr_sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"stderr_bytes\": 0, \"stderr_truncated\": false, \"backend_error\": null}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
